Z||000006||DreXteR||09-26-2001||02:18 PM||||There is a version of the zx3 that is supercharged and makes 300hp.  Not bad for a 4 banger. The look is not bad is just dif also is based in european cars. I like it, for just 17k is good instead +20k for similars type of cars.<P>Btw in the latest rally races the zx3 has beeing in the tops spots takeing down the wrx.   .. . ... .. Brain food.<P><BR>DreX<p>[This message has been edited by DreXteR (edited 09-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||09-26-2001||02:26 PM||||i like em.. i've put nitrous on 3 of them ,2 S/Cs and countless other  mods to them.. check out. ( i've got the same screen name)<BR> <A HREF="http://www.teamfocaljet.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.teamfocaljet.com/</A> <P>i'm all over the forum.. and in Team SR. i've installed the guages, nitrous, exhasut, intaek and a few other things on the NOPI 2nd place winning Saleen Focus.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> they respond well to mods and are easy to drive and seem to hold up really well. <P>the saleen i worked on... <A HREF="http://www.focaljet.com/ubb/Forum45/HTML/000644.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.focaljet.com/ubb/Forum45/HTML/000644.html</A> <P>my friends S/C car... makes 175 at the wheels with 8psi, and 211 on nitrous. we built this car in 4 days.. he wrecked one on a thursday night comming to my house, we had this one that saturday morning, swaped, the suspension, exh, intake, S/C, had a new body kit painted we put it on windows tinted and 300 miles away for a show in pigeon forge, TN the next thursday morning!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.focaljet.com/ubb/Forum45/HTML/000592.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.focaljet.com/ubb/Forum45/HTML/000592.html</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 09-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||09-26-2001||04:19 PM||||The main issue they're concerned with is cost and overall fuel economy.. (I know, nothing fun..)<P>I'm not impressed with the performance at all, it's got nothing until you're past 3/4 throttle, and then the engine revs way up, and the car jumps ahead.. the guy behind me must have thought I was one of those immature guys who just likes to rev their engine, cause this thing was hitting 6,000 RPM every few seconds, but I wasn't holding it there long enough to actually accelerate.. lol<P>yeah, I definitely like 3800 V6s better..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
